*> Implementation test of the "is flat" flag of the spawn info in the client (docs/protocol/05b CommonPlayerSpawnInfo;
*> docs/protocol/56-superflat-world.md §5.3; 12-client-rendering.md §3.3 item 2, §3.4d): Login and Respawn keep the
*> flag in PL-FLAT; the horizon height is the dimension's minY on a flat world and 63 otherwise; the void darkness
*> onset is 1 on a flat world and 32 otherwise, v = clamp((onset + minY - cameraY) / onset, 0, 1); the dark disc is
*> drawn when the eye is below the horizon height and not under water; SKY-UPDATE multiplies the clear colour of a
*> flat world by (1 - v)^2.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-SUPERFLAT-FLAG.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 COPY CLCONST.
 COPY PROTO.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-CONN                BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 256.
 01 WS-ID                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FLAT                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ZERO                BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-ONE                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-LEN                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LONG                BINARY-DOUBLE VALUE 0.
 01 WS-NAME                PIC X(19) VALUE "minecraft:overworld".
 01 WS-EYE                 FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-H                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-V                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SHOWN               PIC 9.
 01 WS-E1                  PIC -(4)9.
 01 WS-E2                  PIC -(4)9.
 01 WS-E3                  PIC -(4)9.
 01 WS-E4                  PIC -(4)9.
 01 WS-R                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-G                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-B                   BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "CL-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     CALL "NET-BUFFERS-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     MOVE PH-PLAY TO CN-PHASE(WS-CONN)

*>   Login with the flag set, Respawn clear, Respawn set, Login clear.
     MOVE 1 TO WS-FLAT
     PERFORM PUT-LOGIN
     CALL "PROTO-PACKET" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN PB-BUFFER WS-ID
     MOVE PL-FLAT TO WS-E1
     MOVE PL-DIM-NAME(1:19) TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "flat Login with Is flat true sets PL-FLAT 1 and the dimension is still read" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) " " PL-DIM-NAME(1:19) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "1 minecraft:overworld" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     MOVE 0 TO WS-FLAT
     PERFORM PUT-RESPAWN
     CALL "PROTO-PACKET" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN PB-BUFFER WS-ID
     MOVE PL-FLAT TO WS-E1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-FLAT
     PERFORM PUT-RESPAWN
     CALL "PROTO-PACKET" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN PB-BUFFER WS-ID
     MOVE PL-FLAT TO WS-E2
     MOVE 0 TO WS-FLAT
     PERFORM PUT-LOGIN
     CALL "PROTO-PACKET" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN PB-BUFFER WS-ID
     MOVE PL-FLAT TO WS-E3
     MOVE "flat Respawn false 0, Respawn true 1, Login false 0 set and clear PL-FLAT" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E2) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E3) DELIMITED BY SIZE
         INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "0 1 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   Horizon height: the dimension's minY on a flat world, else 63 (12 3.4d).
     MOVE -64 TO PL-MIN-Y
     MOVE 1 TO PL-FLAT
     CALL "SKY-HORIZON-HEIGHT" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-H
     MOVE WS-H TO WS-E1
     MOVE 0 TO PL-FLAT
     CALL "SKY-HORIZON-HEIGHT" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-H
     MOVE WS-H TO WS-E2
     MOVE 0 TO PL-MIN-Y
     MOVE 1 TO PL-FLAT
     CALL "SKY-HORIZON-HEIGHT" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-H
     MOVE WS-H TO WS-E3
     MOVE "flat horizon height is minY -64 flat, 63 not flat, minY 0 flat in a dimension from 0" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E2) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E3) DELIMITED BY SIZE
         INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "-64 63 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   Void darkness onset: 1 flat, 32 otherwise (56 5.3).
     MOVE 1 TO PL-FLAT
     CALL "SKY-VOID-ONSET" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-H
     MOVE WS-H TO WS-E1
     MOVE 0 TO PL-FLAT
     CALL "SKY-VOID-ONSET" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-H
     MOVE WS-H TO WS-E2
     MOVE "flat void darkness onset is 1 on a flat world and 32 otherwise" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E2) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "1 32" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   v in thousandths: flat minY -64: camera -58.4 0, -63.5 500, -64 and -70 1000.
     MOVE -64 TO PL-MIN-Y
     MOVE 1 TO PL-FLAT
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE -58.4 TO WS-EYE
     CALL "SKY-VOID-DARKNESS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE WS-V
     MOVE WS-V TO WS-E1
     MOVE -63.5 TO WS-EYE
     CALL "SKY-VOID-DARKNESS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE WS-V
     MOVE WS-V TO WS-E2
     MOVE -64 TO WS-EYE
     CALL "SKY-VOID-DARKNESS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE WS-V
     MOVE WS-V TO WS-E3
     MOVE -70 TO WS-EYE
     CALL "SKY-VOID-DARKNESS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE WS-V
     MOVE WS-V TO WS-E4
     MOVE "flat void darkness on a flat world at camera -58.4, -63.5, -64, -70 is 0, 500, 1000, 1000 thousandths"
         TO TL-CASE
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E2) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E3) " "
         FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E4) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "0 500 1000 1000" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   Not flat (onset 32, minY -64): -32 0, -48 500, -64 1000, 10 0.
     MOVE 0 TO PL-FLAT
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE -32 TO WS-EYE
     CALL "SKY-VOID-DARKNESS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE WS-V
     MOVE WS-V TO WS-E1
     MOVE -48 TO WS-EYE
     CALL "SKY-VOID-DARKNESS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE WS-V
     MOVE WS-V TO WS-E2
     MOVE -64 TO WS-EYE
     CALL "SKY-VOID-DARKNESS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE WS-V
     MOVE WS-V TO WS-E3
     MOVE 10 TO WS-EYE
     CALL "SKY-VOID-DARKNESS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE WS-V
     MOVE WS-V TO WS-E4
     MOVE "flat void darkness of a world that is not flat at camera -32, -48, -64, 10 is 0, 500, 1000, 0"
         TO TL-CASE
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E2) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E3) " "
         FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E4) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "0 500 1000 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   The dark disc: eye - horizon < 0 and not under water.
     MOVE 1 TO PL-FLAT
     MOVE 0 TO PL-EYE-WATER
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE -58.4 TO WS-EYE
     CALL "SKY-DARK-DISC" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE WS-SHOWN
     MOVE WS-SHOWN TO WS-E1
     MOVE -64.5 TO WS-EYE
     CALL "SKY-DARK-DISC" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE WS-SHOWN
     MOVE WS-SHOWN TO WS-E2
     MOVE 1 TO PL-EYE-WATER
     CALL "SKY-DARK-DISC" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE WS-SHOWN
     MOVE WS-SHOWN TO WS-E3
     MOVE 0 TO PL-EYE-WATER
     MOVE 0 TO PL-FLAT
     MOVE 62 TO WS-EYE
     CALL "SKY-DARK-DISC" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE WS-SHOWN
     MOVE WS-SHOWN TO WS-E4
     MOVE "flat dark disc: flat eye -58.4 no, flat eye -64.5 yes, under water no, not flat eye 62 yes" TO TL-CASE
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E2) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E3) " "
         FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E4) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "0 1 0 1" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   The clear colour of a flat world by day (#8FB8E6) is multiplied by (1 - v)^2 with the camera at -63.5
*>   (v 0.5: x 0.25), 0 at -70, and unchanged at -60; a world that is not flat keeps the colour.
     MOVE 1 TO PL-HAS-SKY
     MOVE 6000 TO PL-TIME
     MOVE -64 TO PL-MIN-Y
     MOVE 1 TO PL-FLAT
     MOVE 1.5 TO PL-EYE
     MOVE -65 TO PL-Y
     CALL "SKY-UPDATE" USING CLIENT-STATE
     PERFORM SKY-BYTES
     MOVE WS-R TO WS-E1
     MOVE WS-G TO WS-E2
     MOVE -75 TO PL-Y
     CALL "SKY-UPDATE" USING CLIENT-STATE
     PERFORM SKY-BYTES
     MOVE WS-R TO WS-E3
     MOVE -61.5 TO PL-Y
     CALL "SKY-UPDATE" USING CLIENT-STATE
     PERFORM SKY-BYTES
     MOVE WS-R TO WS-E4
     MOVE "flat sky red and green at camera -63.5 are 36 and 46 (x 0.25), red at -73.5 is 0, red at -60 is 143"
         TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E2) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E3) " "
         FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E4) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "36 46 0 143" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO PL-FLAT
     MOVE -75 TO PL-Y
     CALL "SKY-UPDATE" USING CLIENT-STATE
     PERFORM SKY-BYTES
     MOVE WS-R TO WS-E1
     MOVE "flat sky of a world that is not flat keeps its day colour (red 143) deep below the surface" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "143" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.

 PUT-LOGIN.
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     MOVE 1 TO WS-ID
     MOVE 50 TO WS-ID
     CALL "PB-PUT-INT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ONE
     CALL "PB-PUT-BOOL" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ZERO
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ONE
     MOVE 19 TO WS-LEN
     CALL "PB-PUT-IDENTIFIER" USING PB-BUFFER WS-NAME WS-LEN
     MOVE 20 TO WS-LEN
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-LEN
     MOVE 8 TO WS-LEN
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-LEN
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-LEN
     CALL "PB-PUT-BOOL" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ZERO
     CALL "PB-PUT-BOOL" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ONE
     CALL "PB-PUT-BOOL" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ZERO
     PERFORM PUT-SPAWN-INFO
     CALL "PB-PUT-BOOL" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ZERO
     CALL "PB-PUT-BOOL" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ZERO
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS.

 PUT-RESPAWN.
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     MOVE 84 TO WS-ID
     PERFORM PUT-SPAWN-INFO
     CALL "PB-PUT-UBYTE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ZERO
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS.

 PUT-SPAWN-INFO.
*>   CommonPlayerSpawnInfo (05b): dimension type 0, the dimension, hashed seed, game mode 0, previous game mode
*>   absent, Is debug false, Is flat WS-FLAT, no last death location, portal cooldown 0, sea level 63.
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ZERO
     MOVE 19 TO WS-LEN
     CALL "PB-PUT-IDENTIFIER" USING PB-BUFFER WS-NAME WS-LEN
     CALL "PB-PUT-LONG" USING PB-BUFFER WS-LONG
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ZERO
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ZERO
     CALL "PB-PUT-BOOL" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ZERO
     CALL "PB-PUT-BOOL" USING PB-BUFFER WS-FLAT
     CALL "PB-PUT-BOOL" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ZERO
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ZERO
     MOVE 63 TO WS-LEN
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-LEN.

 SKY-BYTES.
     COMPUTE WS-R ROUNDED = SK-R * 255
     COMPUTE WS-G ROUNDED = SK-G * 255
     COMPUTE WS-B ROUNDED = SK-B * 255.
 END PROGRAM TEST-SUPERFLAT-FLAG.
 COPY CLTEST.
